# Call-site ledger of netaddr at 85a7b25304732785ddee31be3a644a77a243a978.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in netaddr.md.
#
# Types used below. A strategy module (netaddr.strategy.ipv4, ipv6, eui48,
# eui64) is what self._module, addr._module and module hold; its attributes
# (version, width, max_int, family_name, ...) are ints and strs. _value,
# _prefixlen, first, last, size and the results of key() and sort_key() are
# ints and tuples of ints. IPSet._cidrs, SubnetSplitter._subnets and the dicts
# of DictUpdater hold IPNetwork keys (and IPRange and IPAddress keys in the
# multicast dict). The dunder methods of the package classes run only where a
# package object is the operand; the defaults below reject them at every
# other site, and the sites where they run accept them explicitly.
default reject netaddr.core.DictDotLookup.__getitem__, netaddr.core.DictDotLookup.__iter__: no package code subscripts, iterates or searches a DictDotLookup; the package only builds them (registration(), info) and hands them to the client
default reject netaddr.core.DictDotLookup.__repr__: no package code formats a DictDotLookup, except pformat of the __dict__ of a DictDotLookup, whose values can be nested DictDotLookup objects (core.py:185, accepted there)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__getitem__: no package code subscripts, iterates or searches an EUI except self[3:6] and self[3:8] in EUI.ei (accepted there); the operands are ints, strs, bytes, lists, tuples, dicts, sets, re matches, strategy modules or IP objects
default reject netaddr.ip.IPListMixin.__getitem__: no IPNetwork, IPRange or IPGlob is subscripted at this site; the operand is a str, bytes, list, tuple, dict, set, re match, int or a typing-free builtin (the subscripts of IP ranges, such as iterable[0] and cidr[-1], accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__eq__, netaddr.eui.IAB.__eq__, netaddr.eui.OUI.__eq__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__eq__: no package code compares an EUI, OUI, IAB or IPSet, or uses one as a dict key or set element, or searches a container that holds one
default reject netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__eq__: no IP object is compared with == or != or looked up as a dict key or set element at this site; the operands are ints, strs, bytes, tuples of ints, strategy modules, sentinels or None (the IPNetwork-keyed dict and set operations and the comparisons of IP objects accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.BaseIdentifier.__index__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__index__: no EUI or IPAddress is used as an index, a slice bound, a %x, %X or %d operand, or an argument of hex(), bin(), range() or int.to_bytes() at this site; those operands are ints (the hex() of an IPAddress in cli.info accepts the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__hash__, netaddr.eui.OUI.__hash__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__hash__: no package code hashes an EUI, OUI or IPSet or uses one as a dict key or set element; the package's dicts and sets are keyed by ints, strs and IP objects
default reject netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__hash__: no IP object is hashed at this site; the keys and set elements are ints, strs, bytes or tuples of ints (the IPNetwork-keyed dict and set operations accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPListMixin.__iter__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__iter__: no IPNetwork, IPRange, IPGlob or IPSet is iterated, unpacked or searched by iteration at this site; the iterables are strs, bytes, lists, tuples, dicts, sets, generators, re matches and files (the loops over an IPNetwork accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPListMixin.__len__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__len__: no IP range or IPSet is passed to len(), list(), tuple(), sorted() or another builtin that asks for a length at this site; a truth test of these classes calls their __bool__, not __len__
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__ge__, netaddr.eui.EUI.__gt__, netaddr.eui.EUI.__le__, netaddr.eui.EUI.__lt__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__gt__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__lt__: no package code orders EUI objects or IPSets, and no list or tuple of them is sorted, compared or reduced with min() or max()
default reject netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__ge__, netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__gt__, netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__le__, netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__lt__: no IP object is ordered at this site; the operands of <, <=, >, >= and the values that sort(), sorted(), min() and max() order are ints, strs, tuples whose leading int elements decide, or a generator (the comparisons and sorts of IP objects accept the candidates explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__repr__, netaddr.eui.IAB.__repr__, netaddr.eui.OUI.__repr__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__repr__, netaddr.ip.IPNetwork.__repr__, netaddr.ip.IPRange.__repr__, netaddr.ip.glob.IPGlob.__repr__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__repr__: no package object is formatted with %r, !r or repr(), or held in a container that is formatted, at this site; the %r and repr() operands are strs, ints, bytes, tuples of ints, lists of strs, types and client values (pprint_info's %r accepts IPNetwork.__repr__ explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.version, netaddr.ip.BaseIP.version: at this site .version is the int attribute of a strategy module (self._module, addr._module, module), or an int already read and passed as an argument, which the callee does not call; the loads of .version on EUI and IP objects accept the property explicitly
default reject netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__init__: a call that names IPAddress, IPNetwork, IPRange or IPGlob runs that class's own __init__; BaseIP.__init__ runs only through super() in IPAddress.__init__ and IPNetwork.__init__ (accepted there)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__add__: no IPAddress is an operand of + or += at this site; the operands are ints, strs, lists and tuples (cidr[-1] + 1 in IPSet.iscontiguous and self._value + num in IPAddress.__add__ and __iadd__ accept the candidate explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.BaseIdentifier.__int__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__int__: the argument of int() at this site is a str, bytes, int or float, not an EUI, OUI, IAB or IPAddress (the int() calls on package objects accept the candidates explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__str__, netaddr.eui.IAB.__str__, netaddr.eui.OUI.__str__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__str__, netaddr.ip.IPNetwork.__str__, netaddr.ip.IPRange.__str__, netaddr.ip.glob.IPGlob.__str__: no package object is converted with str(), %s, format() or an f-string field at this site; the operands are strs, ints, bytes, tuples, lists, types and client values (the conversions of package objects accept the candidates explicitly)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__rsub__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__sub__: no IPAddress is an operand of - or -= at this site; the operands are ints (self._value - num in IPAddress.__sub__ and __isub__ accepts the candidates explicitly; __rsub__ receives an int num and its num - self._value has no package subtraction callback)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__bool__, netaddr.ip.IPListMixin.__bool__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__bool__: no IP object or IPSet is tested for truth at this site; the tested values are bools, ints, strs, lists, tuples, dicts, sets, re results, None or strategy attributes (isdisjoint's `not result` accepts IPSet.__bool__ explicitly)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPListMixin.__contains__, netaddr.ip.IPNetwork.__contains__, netaddr.ip.IPRange.__contains__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__contains__: the container of this `in` test is a str, bytes, list, tuple, dict, set, dict keys or attrs of a SAX element, not an IP range or IPSet (the `in` tests on IP ranges and IPSets accept the candidates explicitly)
default reject netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__and__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__lshift__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__or__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__rshift__, netaddr.ip.IPAddress.__xor__: every operand of &, |, ^, << and >> (and of &=, |=, ^=, <<=, >>=) in the package is an int (_value, a word, a mask, an int argument) or a flag constant, never an IPAddress
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__ne__, netaddr.eui.IAB.__ne__, netaddr.eui.OUI.__ne__, netaddr.ip.BaseIP.__ne__, netaddr.ip.sets.IPSet.__ne__: no package object is compared with != at this site; the operands are ints, strs, bytes, tuples of ints, lists of strs, dicts or None (cidr[0] != previous in IPSet.iscontiguous accepts BaseIP.__ne__ explicitly)
default reject netaddr.eui.EUI.__setitem__: no package code assigns an item of an EUI; the targets of item assignments are dicts (records, __dict__, the IP dicts) and lists

